ce subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the closed set (or the derivation rule from existing handler signatures) for the 'invocation-adapter kind' route field.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a bounded invocation-adapter kind' is referenced as a route field but the plan never lists the permitted kinds or states how the bound is derived","This is a defaultable gap: the set can be derived from the existing handler invocation signatures being migrated"],"finding":"The 'bounded invocation-adapter kind' set that each route records is never enumerated or given a derivation rule in the plan; an executor must infer the closed set of adapter kinds from existing handler shapes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcc18dceaf0b8e033","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved Architecture, first paragraph ('a bounded invocation-adapter kind')","norm_id":"nf882ed19a4584a76","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor building the route dataclass must decide which adapter kinds exist and risks under- or over-enumerating"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Enumerate the adapter kinds as the distinct invocation signatures observed across the migrated handlers, and state that the enum is closed and validated by the registry unit tests.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","